现在写 security 层：PasswordHasher、JwtUtil、RequireRole、AuthInterceptor、WebConfig。

PasswordHasher 注意 `split("\\$")`：字符串 "pbkdf2$120000$salt$hash" → parts[0]="pbkdf2", [1]="120000", [2]=salt, [3]=hash. Good.

JwtUtil 里 ObjectMapper 写 Map.of 可能顺序无关。verify 解析 payload with `mapper.readValue(decoded, new TypeReference<Map<String,Object>>(){})`. exp 是 Integer/Long → `((Number)claims.get("exp")).longValue()`.

JwtUtil 需要 AppProperties 注入 → constructor.

AuthInterceptor:
```java
@Component
public class AuthInterceptor implements HandlerInterceptor {
  private final JwtUtil jwt;
  public AuthInterceptor(JwtUtil jwt){this.jwt=jwt;}
  @Override public boolean preHandle(...) throws Exception {
    if ("OPTIONS".equalsIgnoreCase(req.getMethod())) return true;
    // public paths
    String path=req.getRequestURI();
    if (path.startsWith("/api/auth/") || path.equals("/api/meta")) return true;
    String header=req.getHeader("Authorization");
    if (header==null || !header.startsWith("Bearer ")) throw new ApiException(UNAUTHORIZED,...);
    JwtClaims c = jwt.verify(header.substring(7));
    RequestContext.setUser(new CurrentUser(c.userId(), c.email(), c.fullName(), c.role()));
    if (handler instanceof HandlerMethod hm) {
      RequireRole ann = hm.getMethodAnnotation(RequireRole.class);
      if (ann==null) ann = hm.getBeanType().getAnnotation(RequireRole.class);
      if (ann!=null && !Set.of(ann.value()).contains(c.role())) throw new ApiException(FORBIDDEN, "Admins only...");
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```
Note: throwing ApiException from interceptor — Spring MVC will route to HandlerExceptionResolver → @RestControllerAdvice handles it? Yes, exceptions from interceptors are processed by DispatcherServlet's HandlerExceptionResolver. Good.

JwtClaims record includes fullName. I'll include name in JWT payload ("name").

WebConfig with CORS.

Also `/health`, `/ready` are outside /api so no interceptor.

