13. UploadService.java

先写纯逻辑类（后面测试要用）。

### OrderRules

```java
package com.webox.service;

public final class OrderRules {
  public record Resolved(LocalDate deliveryDate, String mealPeriod, String notice) {}

  public static String defaultMealPeriod(LocalTime now) {
    if (!now.isBefore(LUNCH_CUTOFF)) return now.isBefore(DINNER_CUTOFF) ? "Dinner" : "Lunch"; // after 15 → next day Lunch
    return "Lunch";
  }

  public static Resolved resolve(LocalDate today, LocalTime now, LocalDate requestedDate, String requestedPeriod) {
    // future dates: accept as-is
    if (requestedDate.isAfter(today)) return new Resolved(requestedDate, normalizedPeriod, "");
    // past dates: reject? handle in service; here clamp to today
    LocalDate date = requestedDate.isBefore(today) ? today : requestedDate;
    String period = normalize(requestedPeriod);
    if (date.isAfter(today)) ...
    if ("Lunch".equals(period) && !now.isBefore(LUNCH_CUTOFF)) {
       if (now.isBefore(DINNER_CUTOFF)) return new Resolved(today,"Dinner","Lunch ordering closes at 10:00. Your order was moved to today's Dinner.");
       return new Resolved(today.plusDays(1),"Lunch","Both of today's meal periods have closed. Your order was moved to tomorrow's Lunch.");
    }
    if ("Dinner".equals(period) && !now.isBefore(DINNER_CUTOFF)) {
       return new Resolved(today.plusDays(1),"Lunch","Dinner ordering closes at 15:00. Your order was moved to tomorrow's Lunch.");
    }
    return new Resolved(date, period, "");
  }
  public static boolean isPortionLimitExceeded(int portions) { return portions > MAX; }
  public static String cutoffNotice(LocalTime now)...
}
```
normalize: if not in MEAL_PERIOD_SET → "Lunch".

Note about "交付日期" after cutoff: when moved to next-day Lunch, deliveryDate changes. Frontend checkout will show notice from response OrderView. Also menu validity uses resolved date; seeded tomorrow menu exists. Good.

### AllergenMatcher
```java
public static List<String> conflicts(Collection<String> dishAllergens, Collection<String> flagged)
public static String warning(List<String> conflicts) -> "This dish contains an allergen you flagged: [Egg]. Add anyway?"
```
Pure.

### PricingService
```java
@Service
public class PricingService {
  private final OptionGroupRepository groups; private final OptionItemRepository items;
  public record PricedLine(long unitCents, List<String> labels) {}

  public Map<Long, List<OptionGroupView>> optionGroupsFor(Collection<Long> dishIds) {...} // used by MenuService
  public PricedLine price(long dishId, long baseCents, List<Long> optionItemIds, List<OptionGroupView> groups) {
     // build allowed ids map from groups
     // validate: no unknown ids, no duplicates, required groups have exactly >=1 selection, maxSelect not exceeded
     // unit = base + sum extras
     // labels = "GroupName: ItemName" strings
  }
}
```
To keep PricingService independent from repositories (for unit tests), make `price` a static pure method taking `List<OptionGroupView>`; and a separate method `loadGroups(dishIds)` in a `DishAssembler` service. I'll design:

`DishAssembler` (service) handles loading option groups/items for dishes and building DishView. MenuService, ConsoleService, OrderService, AiService use it.

PricingService pure static:
```java
public final class PricingService {
  public record PricedLine(long unitCents, List<String> labels) {}
  public static PricedLine price(long baseCents, List<Long> optionItemIds, List<OptionGroupView> groups) { ... }
}
```
Validation messages English, throw ApiException(VALIDATION_ERROR, "...").

For required group: count selected items within group >=1 (and <= maxSelect). Also ensure selected option ids are unique and belong to some group. maxSelect for required groups is 1 typically; for optional group maxSelect 3. Also must not select more than maxSelect.

### MenuCache
```java
@Component
public class MenuCache {
  private final ConcurrentHashMap<String,Entry> map = new ...;
  private final AtomicLong hits/misses/evictions;
  private final long ttlMillis (from props)
  record Entry(Object value, long expiresAt) 
  public Object get(String key), void put(String key, Object value), void invalidateAll(), void invalidateWhere(Predicate<String>)
  public CacheStats stats() {hits, misses, size}
}
```
TTL from AppProperties (seconds). Good.

### DishAssembler
```java
