- toast messages

API client (api.js):
```js
let accessToken = null
export function setToken(t){accessToken=t}
export function getToken(){return accessToken}
const BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE || '/api'

async function request(path, {method='GET', body, headers={}, retry=0, _retryAuth=true}={}) {
  const opts = { method, headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json', ...headers}, credentials:'include' };
  if (accessToken) opts.headers['Authorization'] = `Bearer ${accessToken}`;
  if (body !== undefined) opts.body = JSON.stringify(body);
  let res;
  try { res = await fetch(BASE + path, opts); }
  catch (e) { throw new ApiError('OFFLINE', 'You appear to be offline. Please check your connection.'); }
  if (res.status === 401 && _retryAuth && !path.startsWith('/auth/refresh')) {
     const refreshed = await refreshSession();
     if (refreshed) return request(path,{...}, true?) // retry once
     else throw new ApiError('UNAUTHORIZED','Your session has expired. Please sign in again.')
  }
  if (res.status >= 500 && retry < 3) { await delay(300*(retry+1)); return request(path, {...opts, retry: retry+1}) }  // careful with body serialization
  const json = await res.json().catch(()=>({}));
  if (!res.ok) throw new ApiError(json.error?.code || 'ERROR', friendly(json.error?.message || ...));
  return json.data;
}
```
Need to avoid infinite recursion and preserve body. Let me implement carefully with an internal `doFetch(path, options)` and a wrapper handling retries.

Simpler approach:
```js
export async function api(path, options = {}) {
  for (let attempt=0; attempt<4; attempt++) {
    try {
      const res = await rawFetch(path, options);
      if (res.status === 401 && options.authRetry !== false && !options.skipRefresh) {
         const ok = await refreshSession();
         if (ok) { options = {...options, skipRefresh:true}; continue; }
         clearSession(); throw new ApiError(...);
      }
      if (res.status >= 500 && attempt < 3) { await sleep(400*(attempt+1)); continue; }
      const payload = await res.json();
      if (!res.ok) throw new ApiError(payload?.error?.code, friendlyMessage(payload?.error?.message, res.status));
      return payload.data;
    } catch (e) {
      if (e instanceof ApiError) throw e;
      if (e instanceof TypeError) throw new ApiError('OFFLINE', '...');
      throw new ApiError('ERROR', '...');
    }
  }
}
```
`rawFetch` sets headers; for multipart upload we shouldn't set Content-Type. Add `options.raw` handling.

SSE helper:
```js
export async function stream(path, {method='GET', body, onEvent}) {
  const headers = {'Accept':'text/event-stream'};
  if (body) headers['Content-Type']='application/json';
  if (accessToken) headers['Authorization']=`Bearer ${accessToken}`;
  const res = await fetch(BASE+path, {method, headers, body: body?JSON.stringify(body):undefined, credentials:'include'});
  if (!res.ok) { ... refresh? simplified: if 401 refresh once }
  const reader = res.body.getReader();
  const decoder = new TextDecoder();
  let buffer='';
  while (true) {
    const {value,done} = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    buffer += decoder.decode(value,{stream:true});
    let idx;
    while ((idx = buffer.indexOf('\n\n')) >= 0) {
      const raw = buffer.slice(0,idx); buffer = buffer.slice(idx+2);
      const lines = raw.split('\n');
      let event='message', data='';
      for (const line of lines) {
        if (line.startsWith('event:')) event=line.slice(6).trim();
        else if (line.startsWith('data:')) data += line.slice(5).trim();
      }
      if (data) onEvent(event, data);
    }
  }
}
```
Note: SSE blocks may be separated by `\n\n`; Spring's SseEmitter sends `event:x\ndata:y\n\n`. Also comment lines `:ping` from heartbeat → ignore (data empty). Good.

Need AbortController support for unsubscribing: `stream(path, {signal})` passes signal to fetch; reader.read() will throw on abort → catch and return.

Helper `refreshSession()` calls `/auth/refresh` with credentials, sets token. Must avoid recursion — use raw fetch directly.

Now UI design. Light theme (IDE theme light, but this is an app UI — design clean light). Use a warm green/teal brand (canteen). All text English.

Layout:
- Top nav bar: WeBox logo, nav links (Menu, Orders, Preferences, Console [admin only]), cart badge, user menu / Sign out.
- Mobile: bottom tab bar or hamburger; use responsive CSS with nav wrapping into a bottom bar on small screens.

Menu page:
- Header "Today's Menu" + date + cutoff notice
- Filters: search input (debounced 300ms), multi-select category chips, "Recommend for me" toggle
- Grid of dish cards: image, name, price ¥xx.xx, category tag, spice tag, stock badge ("Only 2 left" / "Sold out"), "Recommended" highlight, Add button (disabled when sold out or cart total >=5)
- Pagination: "Load more" button / page controls (server pagination)
- AI assistant button opens drawer with input and streaming results
- Dish detail modal: description, protein, allergens, spice, option groups (radio for required max 1, checkbox for optional), live price, add to cart with allergen warning dialog
- Allergen warning: modal "This dish contains an allergen you flagged: [Egg]. Add anyway?" with Cancel/Add anyway.
- SSE: on 'stock' events update local menu items remaining; on 'refresh' re-fetch menu.

Cart page:
- list lines with configuration labels, quantity +/- (disabled at 5 total), remove, subtotal, total
- warning when total portions == 5: "Maximum 5 portions per order reached."
- "Proceed to Checkout"

Checkout:
- order summary with options & subtotals
- delivery date (date input, min today), meal period (Lunch/Dinner radio, default from menu), address (datalist of history addresses or new input, maxLength 200)
- budget hint if total > budgetMax
- active order check: if exists show "View Existing Order" button instead of "Place Order"
- Idempotency-Key: generated once per checkout mount (useRef), kept stable across clicks; on success clear cart and go to success page
- errors: insufficient stock with dish names (mapped to friendly message), rule violations
- button disabled during submit (防抖/节流)

Order success: order number, delivery info, notice.

Orders page: list with status chips, View details, Cancel (Pending only).
Order detail modal: items with options, quantity, subtotal, total.

Preferences page: form with allergen checkboxes, cuisine checkboxes, spice select, taste select, budget min/max (in ¥ converted to cents), recommend toggle; save → toast.

Console (admin):
- separate nav layout (PRD: 与员工端使用不同的导航布局) — a sidebar layout with Console header and sections: Dishes, Daily Menu, Dashboard.
- Dishes: table with search/category filter, pagination, Add/Edit dish modal (name, description, price, category, protein, allergens, spice, image upload, active, option groups editor), toggle active.
- Daily Menu: date picker (default tomorrow), list of all dishes with quantity inputs, Save button.
- Dashboard: Today overview cards, Top 10 bar chart (SVG), Lunch vs Dinner (SVG donut or bars), 7-day trend line chart (SVG), low stock list, Refresh button.

Charts: hand-built SVG components (no external deps). Need to handle empty state gracefully.

